From 6b907155ec790c8f424f35470fdfe2b0bd9b7b40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x4pro-emu <kf1178@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 15:03:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] esp32s3.usj: present SOF on every INT_RAW read while a
 host is attached

ESP-IDF's connection monitor clears SOF from the tick hook; bunched ticks made it
declare the host gone and HWCDC then dropped whole lines. A live bus guarantees a
SOF since the last look, so answer that on read.
---
 hw/misc/esp32s3_usj.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/misc/esp32s3_usj.c b/hw/misc/esp32s3_usj.c
index 1c1a7d3..146c080 100644
--- a/hw/misc/esp32s3_usj.c
+++ b/hw/misc/esp32s3_usj.c
@@ -105,6 +105,15 @@ static uint64_t usj_read(void *opaque, hwaddr addr, unsigned int size)
         }
         break;
     case R_INT_RAW:
+        /* A host that is attached sends a SOF every 1 ms. ESP-IDF's connection
+         * monitor checks this bit from the FreeRTOS tick hook and clears it; if
+         * the guest's ticks bunch up (host scheduling) several ticks could see
+         * no SOF and declare the host gone, after which HWCDC drops output.
+         * Present the bit on every read while host-connected: "at least one
+         * SOF since you last looked" is exactly what a live bus guarantees. */
+        if (s->host_connected) {
+            s->int_raw |= INT_SOF;
+        }
         r = s->int_raw;
         break;
     case R_INT_ST:
